    "body": "I think we still need to evaluate whether or not https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-javascript:-url-special-case:document-state-history-policy-container is a valid cloning of the history policy container. If a history policy container should only ever be stored on documents whose URLs are local schemes, and `javascript:` URLs are not local schemes, then we probably shouldn't be cloning here.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, if I understand correctly, the URL of documents resulting from `javascript:` URLs is not a `javascript:` URL, but just a copy of the active document's URL, which may indeed be a URL that requires storing history policy container in the document state, so I think we need the same conditional cloning there as I added in the #create-navigation-params-by-fetching algorithm.",
